  "summary": "Several studies directly apply multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling (Bayesian hierarchical models) to the task of hate speech detection. Adebayo et al. (2026) [V0113] report an AUROC of 0.67 on the ToxiBench dataset. Brennan et al. (2018) [V0114] achieve an F1 score of 0.74 using the GridWatch dataset. Duarte et al. (2020) [V0116] report an MAE of 0.88 on FireScope, while Chen et al. (2019) [V0115] achieve 0.81 accuracy on ProtMap. Other documents mention this method in passing as prior work but apply different methods to hate speech or apply this method to different topics [V0206, V0034, V0173, V0124].",
